HON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nAdd /app/start.sh that stays in the foreground and keeps the cluster serving while alive. Launch three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000, :8001, :8002 and a local redis-server on 127.0.0.1:6379. Implement GET /api/health returning 200 {status:ok, node_id} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports. Self-contained only — no remote services, no Docker-in-Docker. Stub routing so other tasks can attach APIs.\n==== MARATHON-3 ====\nID:       MARATHON-3\nTitle:    Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nImplement POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me per API contract. Username URL-safe slug; password >= 8; 201 {user,token} with token length >= 16; duplicate username 409; invalid input 400; wrong password 401. No email field. Persist users cluster-wide so all three nodes share auth state.\n==== MARATHON-7 ====\nID:       MARATHON-7\nTitle:    Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins list ACL\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nChannelObj fields per contract. POST workspaces/{slug}/channels; join/leave; PATCH topic; members list; archive/unarchive (owner-only); writes to archived → 423. Private join without invite → 403. Duplicate name → 409. Topic max 250. GET pins ACL for private channels.\n==== MARATHON-8 ====\nID:       MARATHON-8\nTitle:    Messages: post, list, edit, delete\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nPOST /api/channels/{id}/messages {body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?} → 201 {message}; empty body → 400. MessageObj fields per contract. GET messages newest-first with limit/before. PATCH body author-only sets edited_at; edit deleted → 409. DELETE author or workspace owner idempotent → 200 {deleted:true}; deleted disappear from listings / reactions stop counting. UTC timestamps; stable ids across cluster.\n==== MARATHON-9 ====\nID:       MARATHON-9\nTitle:    DMs: get-or-create pairwise DM channel\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 1\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nPOST /api/dms {user_id} → 200 {channel_id}. Same channel id both directions and on repeated calls. Channel is_dm true and usable for messages like other channels.\n==== MARATHON-10 ====\nID:       MARATHON-10\nTitle:    Files: upload, metadata, download\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 1\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nPOST /api/files multipart file part → 201 {file: FileObj}. Over 10 MiB → 413. GET /api/files/{id}; GET download with Content-Type and Content-Disposition. Shared across nodes.\n","stderr":"","executionTime":204,"interleavedOutput":"==== MARATHON-2 ====\nID:       MARATHON-2\nTitle:    Cluster scaffold: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis, health\nStatus:   in_progress\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nAssignee: app-architect-1\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nAdd /app/start.sh that stays in the foreground and keeps the cluster serving while alive. Launch three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000, :8001, :8002 and a local redis-server on 127.0.0.1:6379. Implement GET /api/health returning 200 {status:ok, node_id} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports. Self-contained only — no remote services, no Docker-in-Docker. Stub routing so other tasks can attach APIs.\n==== MARATHON-3 ====\nID:       MARATHON-3\nTitle:    Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nImplement POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me per API contract. Username URL-safe slug; password >= 8; 201 {user,token} with token length >= 16; duplicate username 409; invalid input 400; wrong password 401. No email field. Persist users cluster-wide so all three nodes share auth state.\n==== MARATHON-7 ====\nID:       MARATHON-7\nTitle:    Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins list ACL\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nChannelObj fields per contract. POST workspaces/{slug}/channels; join/leave; PATCH topic; members list; archive/unarchive (owner-only); writes to archived → 423. Private join without invite → 403. Duplicate name → 409. Topic max 250. GET pins ACL for private channels.\n==== MARATHON-8 ====\nID:       MARATHON-8\nTitle:    Messages: post, list, edit, delete\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 0\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nPOST /api/channels/{id}/messages {body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?} → 201 {message}; empty body → 400. MessageObj fields per contract. GET messages newest-first with limit/before. PATCH body author-only sets edited_at; edit deleted → 409. DELETE author or workspace owner idempotent → 200 {deleted:true}; deleted disappear from listings / reactions stop counting. UTC timestamps; stable ids across cluster.\n==== MARATHON-9 ====\nID:       MARATHON-9\nTitle:    DMs: get-or-create pairwise DM channel\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 1\nType:     task\nOwner:    marathon-harness\nParent:   MARATHON-1\nLabels:   [architect backend]\n\nDescription:\nPOST /api/dms {user_id} → 200 {channel_id}. Same channel id both directions and on repeated calls. Channel is_dm true and usable for messages like other channels.\n==== MARATHON-10 ====\nID:       MARATHON-10\nTitle:    Files: upload, metadata, download\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 1\nType:     task\nOwner:    mara